\newlabel{app:concept}{{A}{8}{Impact Statement}{section.A}{}}
\newlabel{fig:supp_pc}{{6}{8}{\textbf {Learning reuses the serving computation.} Serving runs the forward pass of a max-plus (tropical) network: in each layer a single winning path is selected and cached (left, blue). Learning is that \emph {same} cached path traversed backward (right, purple)---credit assignment is a gather/scatter/add along routes the forward pass already committed, with no multiplication, no second network, and no stored activation graph. Conceptual companion to Fig.~\ref {fig:arch} and the bitwise-equivalence result of \S \ref {sec:ladder}}{figure.6}{}}
\newlabel{app:opt}{{B}{8}{Impact Statement}{section.B}{}}
\newlabel{tab:opt}{{2}{8}{Multiply-free optimizers vs.\ AdamW (gated drift life, headroom captured; adversary = consecutive-update collapse test). Data: \texttt {v4\_life}, \texttt {v4\_tele\_precut\_*}}{table.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:supp_depth}{{7}{9}{\textbf {Predictive coding, made stable at depth.} Naively settling the states of a deep predictive-coding network amplifies error with depth: the dynamics diverge and accuracy collapses to chance (left). Our substrate instead relaxes the \emph {errors} with routing frozen---triangular, hence unconditionally stable---and collapses to a single multiply-free reverse sweep that stays accurate to 128 layers (right). Conceptual companion to the cascade $\equiv $ backprop equivalence and the depth-scaling results}{figure.7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:supp_org}{{8}{9}{\textbf {A persistent living system versus the conventional split.} Left: our loop is one always-on process on its stream of experience, serving every input and---when surprised---learning in place at energy below the measurement floor; the experience \emph {is} the training, and every update is auditable. Right: the deployed norm keeps a model current with a separate, power-hungry training cluster that periodically ships a frozen snapshot to a distinct serving system, coupled by synchronization and replay storage (\S \ref {sec:agent})}{figure.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:efabl}{{9}{10}{\textbf {Error feedback cures the sign-SGD collapse.} Held-LR, every-window-kicks, stationary, anchorless adversary: naked \texttt {PureTropicalSGD} and a soft-bound-only variant diverge while the error-feedback arms stay flat at zero regret and constant norm ($2{\times }2$ ablation; the cure is error feedback, not the soft-bound). Fully multiply-free. Data: \texttt {v4\_tele\_precut\_*}}{figure.9}{}}
